d009fb786d36a6cab4a7d410630b9382992faa08:.claude/science/exercises/gravity-current-state-20261009/agents/RC_C1_referee.md:9:3. **Theorem A:** The scalar reduction works, but strictly yields \(E^2=m_0^2+\beta |k|^2\) with nonzero real \(\beta\); writing \(\beta=c^2>0\) needs positive curvature/minimum at \(k=0\). Extension through the exceptional set also needs continuity on all \(U\). Smooth persistent taste degeneracies are covered, isolated crossings are not. Mutually scattering self-scatterers share \(\beta\), since an AB collision gives \((\beta_A-\beta_B)(k_1-k_3)=0\). Common \(\beta\) propagates only through nondegenerate mutual-scattering edges; “every scattering mediator” is too broad because interspecies-only scattering is admitted as unproved. [C1_report.md:118–147](</private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes--claude-worktrees-toe-leverage-analysis-e8a790/af5789b9-888d-43b1-90de-58a07e0f2129/scratchpad/laneRC/ref_C1/C1_report.md:118>)
d009fb786d36a6cab4a7d410630b9382992faa08:.claude/science/exercises/gravity-current-state-20261009/agents/RC_C1_referee_full.md:11:3. **Theorem A -- scalar core confirmed with three scope corrections; common speed is proved only along the stated scattering graph.**  Componentwise Lemma R gives `E grad E=aE+Bk+c`; symmetry of the Hessian forces `a=0` unless the gradient image lies in an affine line, and proper cubic covariance excludes such a nonconstant line image and reduces `B` to a scalar and `c` to zero (`C1_report.md:118-132`).  Strictly the conclusion is `E^2=m_0^2+beta|k|^2` with nonzero real `beta`; writing `beta=c^2>0` needs the additional physical hypothesis that the branch has positive curvature/minimum at the origin.  Extension across the exceptional set `S` also needs continuity of the band on all of `U`, not merely the displayed regularity on `U\S`.  Once `beta != 0`, conservation makes every nonzero-umklapp amplitude vanish because its vector-charge defect is `2pi beta m`.  For a smooth, persistently degenerate taste block, Lemma D makes the current `E grad E` times the identity, so the scalar argument applies; an isolated crossing or a non-smooth projector is not such a block.  If A and B each self-scatter, their forms are `f_A=beta_A k`, `f_B=beta_B k`; any nonzero-transfer AB collision gives `(beta_A-beta_B)(k_1-k_3)=0`, hence `beta_A=beta_B`.  Thus the common coefficient claim at `C1_report.md:139` is correct but should have included this one-line proof.  It propagates only through connected nondegenerate mutual-scattering edges.  The stronger sentence that every scattering mediator is SLAC with one common speed overreaches the report's own admission that interspecies-only scattering is merely argued (`C1_report.md:136-147`), and it does not cover gapless sectors lacking sharp asymptotic bands.
d009fb786d36a6cab4a7d410630b9382992faa08:.claude/science/exercises/gravity-current-state-20261009/agents/RC_C1_referee_full.md:19:7. **Fixed verdict -- bounded FAIL, not INCONCLUSIVE.**  The fixed rule asks whether the reduction holds and exact realization is impossible for the explicitly stated finite-component quadratic class (`TESTS.md:1107-1110,1129-1134`).  After the regular-shell and band-continuity qualifications above, the scalar reduction holds, and B1 completely closes that quadratic analytic class.  The two-band sequence never gives an exact finite network, while gapless-mediator dressed bands are an additional interacting class that the report openly leaves unresolved.  A no-go scope stress test therefore leaves the following honest boundary: finite analytic matrices are closed; analytic simple dressed roots are closed at a gapped face; band touchings evade the single-band approximation floor but not exact B1; gapless continua, transfer-singular `R^{-d}` improvements, open-set scattering zeros, interspecies-only matrix scattering, and `d=1` reduction remain unclosed.  Those routes forbid the report's broad “no finite network” shorthand but do not change the registered finite-component-quadratic FAIL criterion.
d009fb786d36a6cab4a7d410630b9382992faa08:.claude/science/exercises/gravity-current-state-20261009/agents/RC_C1_referee_full.md:23:Under transfer-regular improvement kernels, additive exact asymptotic conservation, a regular full-support normal-collision relation in `d>=2`, and a continuous isolated scalar band with noncollinear gradient image, closure forces `E^2=m_0^2+beta|k|^2` on the lifted zone and forces nonzero-umklapp amplitudes to vanish; cubic symmetry alone fixes scalar `beta` but not its positive sign.  Smooth persistent taste degeneracies inherit the same scalar symbol, and self-scattering species connected by nondegenerate mutual scattering share `beta`, while crossings, interspecies-only scattering, and gapless non-particle sectors are not covered.  No finite-component periodic real-analytic one-body matrix in any `d>=1` can possess that exact SLAC eigenvalue, and a simple jointly analytic dressed root cannot carry its face cusp; with a positive-spectral-weight scalar self-energy this excludes any face point where the continuum remains strictly gapped, but not a gapless continuum.  For one smooth band the best whole-zone `E^2` error is `Theta(1/n)` (numerically `1.7603/n`) and the closure residual is at least `pi c^2`; window errors have the stated Bernstein--Walsh exponents, while the fixed global-boundedness constraint is numerically nonbinding only over the resolved range.  A face-touching two-band construction genuinely improves whole-zone error and residual super-algebraically at finite range, but is never exact at finite range and leaves, rather than proves, the partner-band interaction obstruction.  Therefore the unchanged fixed reading is **C1 FAIL, bounded to finite-component analytic quadratic networks (and the stated analytic simple-root dressed subclass)**, with gapless-mediator dressed bands and singular improvements remaining open.
